If you're preparing for **real-time Spring Boot Microservices projects and interviews**, these are the **most used Spring, Spring Boot, Hibernate/JPA annotations** along with practical syntax and usage.

# 1. Spring Core Annotations

## @Component

Creates a Spring-managed bean.

```java
@Component
public class EmailUtil {

    public void sendMail() {
        System.out.println("Mail Sent");
    }
}
```

***

## @Service

Business logic layer.

```java
@Service
public class EmployeeService {

    public String getEmployee() {
        return "Employee Data";
    }
}
```

***

## @Repository

Database layer.

```java
@Repository
public interface EmployeeRepository extends JpaRepository<Employee, Long> {

}
```

***

## @Autowired

Dependency Injection.

```java
@Service
public class EmployeeService {

    @Autowired
    private EmployeeRepository repository;
}
```

Constructor Injection (recommended in projects):

```java
@Service
public class EmployeeService {

    private final EmployeeRepository repository;

    public EmployeeService(EmployeeRepository repository) {
        this.repository = repository;
    }
}
```

***

# 2. Spring Boot Annotations

## @SpringBootApplication

Main class annotation.

```java
@SpringBootApplication
public class EmployeeApplication {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(EmployeeApplication.class, args);
    }
}
```

Equivalent to:

```java
@Configuration
@EnableAutoConfiguration
@ComponentScan
```

***

## @Configuration

Configuration class.

```java
@Configuration
public class AppConfig {

    @Bean
    public RestTemplate restTemplate() {
        return new RestTemplate();
    }
}
```

***

## @Bean

Creates bean manually.

```java
@Bean
public ModelMapper modelMapper() {
    return new ModelMapper();
}
```

***

# 3. REST API Annotations

## @RestController

Used in Microservices APIs.

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/employees")
public class EmployeeController {

}
```

***

## @RequestMapping

Base URL mapping.

```java
@RequestMapping("/api/v1")
```

***

## @GetMapping

```java
@GetMapping("/{id}")
public Employee getEmployee(@PathVariable Long id){
    return service.getEmployee(id);
}
```

***

## @PostMapping

```java
@PostMapping
public Employee saveEmployee(@RequestBody Employee employee){
    return service.save(employee);
}
```

***

## @PutMapping

```java
@PutMapping("/{id}")
public Employee updateEmployee(
        @PathVariable Long id,
        @RequestBody Employee employee){
    return service.update(id, employee);
}
```

***

## @DeleteMapping

```java
@DeleteMapping("/{id}")
public String delete(@PathVariable Long id){
    service.delete(id);
    return "Deleted";
}
```

***

## @PathVariable

```java
@GetMapping("/{id}")
public Employee get(@PathVariable Long id){
    return service.get(id);
}
```

***

## @RequestParam

```java
@GetMapping
public List<Employee> search(
       @RequestParam String department){
    return service.search(department);
}
```

URL:

```text
/employees?department=IT
```

***

## @RequestBody

```java
@PostMapping
public Employee save(@RequestBody Employee employee){
     return service.save(employee);
}
```

JSON:

```json
{
  "name":"John",
  "salary":50000
}
```

***

# 4. Validation Annotations

Real-time projects heavily use validation.

## @Valid

```java
@PostMapping
public Employee save(@Valid @RequestBody Employee employee){
    return service.save(employee);
}
```

***

## @NotNull

```java
@NotNull
private String name;
```

***

## @NotBlank

```java
@NotBlank
private String email;
```

***

## @Size

```java
@Size(min=3,max=50)
private String name;
```

***

## @Email

```java
@Email
private String email;
```

