# 5. Hibernate / JPA Annotations

## @Entity

```java
@Entity
public class Employee {

}
```

***

## @Table

```java
@Entity
@Table(name="employee")
public class Employee {

}
```

***

## @Id

```java
@Id
private Long id;
```

***

## @GeneratedValue

```java
@Id
@GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
private Long id;
```

***

## @Column

```java
@Column(name="employee_name")
private String name;
```

***

## @Transient

Will not create DB column.

```java
@Transient
private String tempData;
```

***

## @CreationTimestamp

```java
@CreationTimestamp
private LocalDateTime createdDate;
```

***

## @UpdateTimestamp

```java
@UpdateTimestamp
private LocalDateTime updatedDate;
```

***

# 6. Relationship Mapping Annotations

## One To One

```java
@OneToOne
@JoinColumn(name="address_id")
private Address address;
```

***

## One To Many

```java
@OneToMany(mappedBy = "department")
private List<Employee> employees;
```

***

## Many To One

Most common in projects.

```java
@ManyToOne
@JoinColumn(name="department_id")
private Department department;
```

***

## Many To Many

```java
@ManyToMany
@JoinTable(
 name = "employee_project",
 joinColumns=@JoinColumn(name="employee_id"),
 inverseJoinColumns=@JoinColumn(name="project_id"))
private List<Project> projects;
```

***

# 7. Transaction Management

## @Transactional

```java
@Transactional
public Employee saveEmployee(Employee employee){
    return repository.save(employee);
}
```

If an exception occurs, the transaction rolls back.

***

# 8. Microservices Annotations

## @EnableDiscoveryClient

Register service with Eureka.

```java
@SpringBootApplication
@EnableDiscoveryClient
public class EmployeeServiceApplication {

}
```

***

## @FeignClient

Inter-service communication.

```java
@FeignClient(name = "DEPARTMENT-SERVICE")
public interface DepartmentClient {

    @GetMapping("/departments/{id}")
    DepartmentDto getDepartment(@PathVariable Long id);
}
```

***

## Circuit Breaker (Resilience4j)

```java
@CircuitBreaker(name="departmentService",
fallbackMethod="fallbackResponse")
public DepartmentDto getDepartment(Long id){

}
```

```java
public DepartmentDto fallbackResponse(Long id, Exception ex){
    return new DepartmentDto();
}
```

